<Layout
  title="Terms of Service – Online Copy Paste"
  description="Read the Terms of Service for using Online Copy Paste, a temporary browser-based text transfer tool."
>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300 dark:hover:text-amber-200">&larr; Back to Online Copy Paste</a>
    <article class="mt-8 prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert prose-lg">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 4, 2026</p>
      <p>These Terms of Service govern your use of <strong>Online Copy Paste</strong> at <strong>onlinecopypaste.com</strong>. By using the website or its clipboard transfer API, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the service.</p>

      <h2>What the Service Does</h2>
      <p>Online Copy Paste lets you transfer text between devices through a browser. You paste text on one device, generate a temporary six-digit code, enter the code on another device, and copy the retrieved text. The service is intended for temporary transfers of text, links, notes, messages, addresses, and small code snippets.</p>
      <p>Each transfer is limited to 20,000 characters. Transfer records expire 10 minutes after creation or are deleted after a successful one-time retrieval. The service does not provide permanent storage, file transfer, image transfer, synchronization, or backup.</p>

      <h2>Your Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>You are responsible for the text you submit and for keeping your transfer code reasonably private. Anyone who obtains a valid code may be able to retrieve the associated text before it expires. Check the retrieved text before using it, especially when transferring a link, command, address, or code.</p>
      <p>Use the service only for lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Submit content that violates applicable law or another person’s rights.</li>
        <li>Attempt to access transfers without authorization or guess codes at scale.</li>
        <li>Use the service to distribute malware, phishing content, spam, or abusive material.</li>
        <li>Interfere with the website, API, database, hosting infrastructure, or another user’s access.</li>
        <li>Use automated requests in a way that creates unreasonable load or bypasses controls.</li>
        <li>Submit secrets or highly sensitive information when a more appropriate secure channel is available.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Availability and Changes</h2>
      <p>We work to keep Online Copy Paste available, but the service may be interrupted for maintenance, provider outages, security response, network failures, or circumstances outside our control. We may change, suspend, or discontinue features, including the transfer duration or character limit, when reasonably necessary to operate the service.</p>
      <p>Do not rely on Online Copy Paste as your only copy of important information. A transfer can expire, be retrieved by someone with the code, or fail before completion.</p>

      <h2>Content and Abuse Reports</h2>
      <p>You retain responsibility for content you submit. You grant us and our infrastructure providers the limited permission needed to process, transmit, store temporarily, retrieve, and delete that content to provide the requested transfer.</p>
      <p>If you believe the service is being used for abuse or unlawful activity, email <a href="mailto:contact@onlinecopypaste.com">contact@onlinecopypaste.com</a> with the relevant code or URL if safe to share. Do not email passwords, private keys, or the contents of sensitive material.</p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what information the service processes and how temporary transfers are handled. By using the service, you acknowledge that text submitted for a transfer must be sent to our application infrastructure so the second device can retrieve it.</p>

      <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, Online Copy Paste is provided on an “as available” basis without a guarantee that every transfer will be uninterrupted, error-free, secure, or suitable for a particular purpose. We do not promise that transferred content will always be available, unaltered, or delivered within a particular time.</p>
      <p>Nothing in these terms removes rights or remedies that cannot legally be excluded in your location.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, we are not responsible for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or loss-of-data damages arising from your use of or inability to use the service. This includes losses caused by an expired transfer, an exposed code, a provider outage, or reliance on transferred content.</p>

      <h2>Changes and Contact</h2>
      <p>We may revise these terms as the service develops. The effective date above identifies the current version. Questions about these terms should be sent to <a href="mailto:contact@onlinecopypaste.com">contact@onlinecopypaste.com</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
